{
  "description": "CRITICAL: Ownership relationships must be unidirectional. If A owns B, B should not own A. References can be bidirectional, but ownership is one-way. Lowest component owns state; higher levels reference. Avoid circular ownership.",
  "scanner": "agile_bot.bots.base_bot.src.actions.validate.scanners.unidirectional_ownership_scanner.UnidirectionalOwnershipScanner",
  "examples": [
    {
      "do": {
        "description": "Ensure unidirectional ownership",
        "content": [
          "Ownership is one-way: owner → owned",
          "References can be bidirectional, but ownership is not",
          "Lowest component owns state; higher levels reference",
          "Show ownership with 'Has X' and references with 'References X'",
          "",
          "Correct Examples (unidirectional ownership):",
          "",
          "Block",
          "    Has violations: Violation",
          "    References file: File",
          "    (Block owns violations, references file)",
          "",
          "Violation",
          "    References rule: Rule",
          "    References block: Block",
          "    References scan: Scan",
          "    (Violation references but doesn't own - owned by Block/Scan)",
          "",
          "File",
          "    Has blocks: Block",
          "    (File owns blocks)",
          "",
          "Block",
          "    References file: File",
          "    (Block references file, doesn't own it)",
          "",
          "Scan",
          "    Has violations: Violation",
          "    (Scan collects violations - unique scan instance)",
          "",
          "Domain Model Pattern:",
          "Owner",
          "    Has owned: OwnedType",
          "",
          "Referencer",
          "    References referenced: ReferencedType",
          "",
          "Owned",
          "    References owner: OwnerType (reference, not ownership)"
        ]
      },
      "dont": {
        "description": "Don't create bidirectional ownership",
        "content": [
          "Don't create circular ownership (A owns B, B owns A)",
          "Don't confuse references with ownership",
          "Don't place ownership at wrong level",
          "",
          "Wrong Examples (bidirectional ownership):",
          "",
          "Block",
          "    Has violations: Violation",
          "    Has file: File",
          "",
          "File",
          "    Has blocks: Block",
          "    Has violations: Violation",
          "    (Circular: File owns Block, Block owns File - WRONG)",
          "",
          "Rule",
          "    Has violations: Violation",
          "",
          "Violation",
          "    Has rule: Rule",
          "    (Circular: Rule owns Violation, Violation owns Rule - WRONG)",
          "",
          "Scope",
          "    Has violations: Violation",
          "",
          "Violation",
          "    Has scope: Scope",
          "    (Wrong level - violations owned by Block/Scan, not Scope)",
          "",
          "Unidirectional Ownership Violation Indicators (REJECT):",
          "- Circular ownership (A owns B, B owns A)",
          "- Confusing references with ownership",
          "- Ownership at wrong level (higher level owning what lower level should own)",
          "- Bidirectional 'Has' relationships",
          "",
          "Key Distinction:",
          "- 'Has X' = Ownership (one-way)",
          "- 'References X' = Reference (can be bidirectional)",
          "- Ownership flows down hierarchy (parent owns child)",
          "- References can point in any direction"
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}

